==English==

===Etymology===
{{w|Analytic language|Analytic form}} of the earlier {{m|en|overget}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-get over.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|<,,got,got[UK]:gotten[US]>}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|transitive}} To [[overcome]].
#: {{ux|en|I'm trying to '''get over''' my fear of flying.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|transitive}} To [[recover]] (from).
#: {{ux|en|I'm having problems '''getting over''' a bad cold.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|transitive}} To [[forget]] and [[move on]]; to [[calm down]] regarding something.
#: {{ux|en|She was in love with me for 10 years, and still hasn't '''got over''' the fact that the feeling wasn't mutual.}}
#* {{quote-song |en |year=1996 |author=w:Jerry Cantrell | artist=w:Alice in Chains |title=Killer Is Me |album={{w|Unplugged (Alice in Chains album)|Unplugged}} |url=https://music.youtube.com/watch?v=JztnWfB3sfY |passage=Oh yeah <br/>Can I start over? <br/>Oh yeah <br/>Can I start over? <br/>and '''get over''' it <br/>}}
# {{lb|en|slang|transitive}} To manipulate (someone); to [[get around]] (someone); to [[improve]] one's own standing at another's expense.
#: {{ux|en|We need a plan to '''get over''' Mr. Smith.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|transitive}} To successfully communicate; to [[get across]].
#: {{ux|en|In our lectures we need to '''get over''' the importance of online safety.}}
# {{lb|en|rugby}} To score a [[try]].
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=February 13, 2011
|author=Lyle Jackson
|title=Ireland 22-25 France
|work=BBC
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/rugby_union/9396342.stm
|page=
|passage=Ireland got their second try not long before half-time with O'Leary, an injury doubt all week with a stiff back, just about '''getting over''' for a try which was confirmed by the video referee.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251113040012/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/rugby_union/9396342.stm|archivedate=13 November 2025}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=October 28 2023|author=Leighton Koopman|work={{w|Independent Online}}|title=YES!!! The Springboks beat the All Blacks to win another Rugby World Cup title|url=https://www.iol.co.za/sport/rugby/rugby-world-cup-2023/yes-the-springboks-beat-the-all-blacks-to-win-another-rugby-world-cup-title-a52cdff9-2db5-495f-b3fe-f02f6f4fd441|passage=But when a side plays for almost 20 of the first 40 minutes with only 14 men, you have to make that advantage count in your favour. Credit must go to the three-time champions for keeping the world champions from '''getting over''' for five points.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250210172602/https://www.iol.co.za/sport/rugby/rugby-world-cup-2023/yes-the-springboks-beat-the-all-blacks-to-win-another-rugby-world-cup-title-a52cdff9-2db5-495f-b3fe-f02f6f4fd441|archivedate=10 February 2025}}
# {{lb|en|slang|intransitive}} To [[impress]] someone; to achieve a goal; to be successful.
#: {{ux|en|The concert went well, and we really '''got over''' with the talent scout.}}
# {{lb|en|professional wrestling|_|slang}} To establish a [[connection]] with the [[audience]] as a character or faction.
# {{lb|en|slang|intransitive|transitive}} To use a drug one is addicted to; to provide an addict with a dose.
#: {{ux|en|She needs to '''get over''' every day.}}
#: {{ux|en|He can '''get''' me '''over'''.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|intransitive|AAVE}} To have sex.

